  "name": "sine_duel_a",
  "description": "A sine that fights its note: a nearly pure self-oscillator only loosely forced by its note, so each note slides in from up to a semitone away and settles; its grip loosens now and then (48 s LFO) and it slips towards its own detuned pitch before relocking; each note sits a few cents off and wavers slowly (per-note LFO and random offset), so unisons and seconds against the other duellist beat and pull. Cold, narrow: one partial, a faint second harmonic glints on a 19 s MSEG. Then a resonant comb fixed on E2 (82.4 Hz): notes on its teeth ring (E, B), the others (D, C, F) sound hollower; it wanders slowly (21 s LFO) so every slide and waver rings through it.",
